The '''Stone Eye''' resembles the {{e|Bloodshot Eye}}. It constantly rotates in a clockwise circle and shoots a flickering {{i|Technology}} laser. It stops firing after the room is cleared. Unlike any other Stone Grimace variants, the Stone Eye appears to despawn when the room is cleared, exited, and then re-entered. {{dlc|r+}} Stone Eyes will do an entire rotation before shooting their laser.
{{clear}}

=== Bomb Grimace ===
{{infobox monster
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Bomb Grimace
 | id          = 809
 | environment = {{floor|Mines}}{{floor|Ashpit}}<br>{{room|boss}}{{room|boss challenge}}<br>{{room|treasure}} ([[Mines]] and [[Ashpit]] only)
 | behavior    = Stationary and invulnerable monster that coughs up a {{E|Throwable Bomb}} if one doesn't exist already. If destroyed by any means, 10 Throwable Bombs are dropped.
}}

The '''Bomb Grimace''' is a unique Stone Grimace in that its only purpose is to keep a single {{E|Throwable Bomb}} spawned. A few seconds after Isaac takes the bomb, it will spawn another.

If it is destroyed with an instant-death attack such as {{i|Euthanasia}} or {{i|Little Horn}}, it spawns 10 Throwable Bombs.

Always spawns during the battle of {{e|Tuff Twins}} and {{e|The Shell}}. It can also appear in the mineshaft in Mines/Ashpit II, where the Throwable Bombs it provides prove essential for fleeing {{e|Mother's Shadow}}.
{{clear}}

=== Quake Grimace ===
{{infobox monster
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Quake Grimace
 | id          = 804
 | environment = {{floor|Mines}}{{floor|Ashpit}}
 | behavior    = Stationary and invulnerable monster that jumps and fires a line of rocks in one direction upon landing.
